// Embedded, hand-subsetted Noto Sans (OFL-licensed) TTF, base64-encoded, for
// the PDF export (app.js) — jsPDF's built-in standard fonts (Helvetica etc.)
// only cover the WinAnsi/Latin-1 codepage, which does NOT include Romanian's
// comma-below diacritics (\u0219 \u021b, and their uppercase forms) at all,
// and is missing \u0103 (a-breve) too — those glyphs silently render as
// blank space with the default font. Embedding a real font is the only fix;
// jsPDF has no way to fall back to a system font for missing glyphs.
//
// Subsetted (fontTools, not committed here) from Google's variable "Noto
// Sans[wdth,wght]" down to Basic Latin + Latin-1 Supplement + Latin
// Extended-A/B + general punctuation (em/en dash, curly quotes) + the Euro
// sign — everything the app's English/Romanian export copy can produce,
// nothing else. Tables trimmed to exactly what jsPDF's own minimal
// TTF/OpenType parser expects: cmap/glyf/loca/head/hhea/hmtx/maxp/post/OS2
// plus a `name` table keeping IDs 1/2/3/4/6 (family/subfamily/unique-id/
// full-name/PostScript-name) — GSUB/GPOS/GDEF/STAT and every variable-font
// table (fvar/avar/gvar/HVAR/MVAR/cvar) explicitly dropped. jsPDF's parser
// isn't a full OpenType implementation: it throws ("Cannot read properties
// of undefined (reading '0'/'widths')") on the leftover variable-font/
// layout tables, and separately needs the font's PostScript name (name ID
// 6) to actually register glyph metrics — an empty/stripped name table
// fails that silently, which is what earlier attempts at this subset got
// wrong. Verified end-to-end against the exact jsPDF 3.0.1 + jspdf-autotable
// 5.0.8 UMD bundles this app loads from CDN (see index.html), not just
// visually — rendered a real PDF (via jsdom, loading the identical CDN
// bytes) and extracted its text with pdftotext to confirm every Romanian
// diacritic round-trips correctly, in both plain text and autoTable cells.
//
// ~40KB per weight. Loaded once per export via registerPdfFonts(doc) (see
// app.js) using jsPDF's addFileToVFS/addFont — no network fetch, no CSP/CDN
// involvement, cached by the service worker like any other same-origin
// asset after the first load.
export const NOTO_SANS_REGULAR_B64 =
  "";

export const NOTO_SANS_BOLD_B64 =
  "";
